      "content": "To calculate straight-line depreciation, first find the depreciable cost by subtracting the salvage value from the initial cost: $\\$45,000 - \\$5,000 = \\$40,000$. Next, divide the depreciable cost by the useful life in years: $\\$40,000 / 8 \\text{ years} = \\$5,000$. Therefore, the annual straight-line depreciation expense for your equipment is \\$5,000.",
